Indy the archaeologist quaffed a cursed potion of booze (I was all set
to rustproof my hard hat).  It made me go blind. This character has been
blind for a long time (2000+ turns). I have repeatedly cast my "cure
blindness" spell -- I get no message when I do so.  I have quaffed a potion
of extra healing.  I have prayed (when I was neither low on hit points
or starving) and my god hasn't helped me.  I have never been blinded this
long before, and not be able to cast my way out of it.  I even quaffed a
potion of sickness in the vain hope it would shock my retinas into working.
Fortunately I had a spare tin of floating eye meat on me which kept my
telepathy up in the face of cursin' baddies.  But an ochre jelly almost
punched my ticket.

So my 11th level b-rp Excalibur wielding archaelogist is permanently blind?
Say it ain't so!  Say it ain't so!  Can Indy get corneal transplants?

